    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. We've had some close calls lately with loads shifting unexpectedly during forklift movement. Even when we follow the patterns, sometimes a stack just seems to tilt or get disturbed for no obvious reason. Is there anything specific we should look for to identify why a load might become unstable before it actually fails?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
