      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To identify potential instability, inspect the stack regularly, looking for signs like small movements or uneven wear on the load's fittings and strapping, indicating a settlement or shifting of the load. Also, check for 'kicking point' warning signs where a portion of the load touches other parts of the stack - this is often a weak point in the interlocking pattern. By spotting these issues before they cause a failure, you can take preventative action and early warn the forklift operators.",
